00:00:18.517 --> 00:00:19.686
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:22.554
-I'm Pam and I'm here
to entertain.

00:00:22.554 --> 00:00:23.890
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:26.125
-There's nothing you're
gonna see in a movie

00:00:26.125 --> 00:00:27.593
that's gonna screw you up!
-[Laughing]

00:00:27.593 --> 00:00:28.927
-Oh, my gosh!

00:00:28.927 --> 00:00:31.430
-When you go that hard,
you have to take a breather.

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:32.932
-You have to take a breather.

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:36.235
-I think this character and my
enjoyment in this character,

00:00:36.235 --> 00:00:38.638
wearing a helmet
is directly equivalent

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:40.273
with my ambition
in this business.

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:41.474
-[Laughs]
-Most people be like,

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:43.442
"I want my face to show
in 'Star Wars'!"

00:00:43.442 --> 00:00:45.211
I'm like, "No,
this is perfect for me."

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:46.746
-Yeah.
-This is exactly the level

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:48.213
I wanna be in "Star Wars."

00:00:48.213 --> 00:00:50.550
-You got to work with
a up-and-comer in that scene.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.718
-Both: Yeah.
-We basically forced her

00:00:52.718 --> 00:00:54.654
into a hug
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:54.654 --> 00:00:56.856
[ Laughter ]
and just said thank you.

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:57.924
-And what do you think
the odds are

00:00:57.924 --> 00:00:59.659
that she went directly to HR?

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:01.560
-I mean, because she's
a newcomer, I don't know.

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:02.861
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:01:02.861 --> 00:01:04.430
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:06.399
-This is Robert Mueller
and he's like,

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:08.534
"My report is 400 pages long."

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:10.703
And then, this is William Barr
and he's like,

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:12.438
"Here's my summary.
It's a Post-It note."

00:01:12.438 --> 00:01:13.606
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.606 --> 00:01:15.341
-And then, this is Congress
and they're like,

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:16.876
"We're too busy to read it."

00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:19.311
And then, Elizabeth Warren's
like, "Not me, bitches!"

00:01:19.311 --> 00:01:21.747
-Oh, right.
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:21.747 --> 00:01:23.383
Do you have time
to keep up with politics?

00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:24.684
Are you paying attention
to the election?

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:28.721
-I've paid enough attention
that I can tell this joke

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:30.990
or I can take a closer look!

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:34.326
[ Suspenseful theme plays ]
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:34.326 --> 00:01:38.364
-To impeach a president
who 63 million people voted for

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:42.802
over eight lines in a call
transcript is baloney.

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:44.103
[ Laughter ]
-Oh.

00:01:44.103 --> 00:01:46.072
[as Castor]
It's, uh, ba-lo-ney!

00:01:46.072 --> 00:01:48.675
[ Laughter and applause ]
Really loses the drama

00:01:48.675 --> 00:01:51.444
when the word you're ramping
up to is baloney.

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:53.712
[ Laughter ]
You know, you never hear

00:01:53.712 --> 00:01:55.415
a detective in a mystery
novel saying,

00:01:55.415 --> 00:01:57.750
[French accent] "I've deduced
that the suspect's alibi is,

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:58.951
um, baloney!"

00:01:58.951 --> 00:02:02.222
[ Laughter and applause ]
You are a 73-year-old man

00:02:02.222 --> 00:02:04.290
attacking a 16-year-old activist

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:05.825
because she cares
about the environment.

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:06.826
Think about how sad that is.

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:08.394
You are a husk of a man.

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:10.263
Actually, not even. For there
to be a husk of a man,

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:12.598
there would've had to have
been a man to begin with.

00:02:12.598 --> 00:02:14.500
You're a husk of a husk.
You're a Russian

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:16.001
nesting doll of husks.

00:02:16.001 --> 00:02:17.002
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:17.002 --> 00:02:18.004
-"How could you let

00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:19.438
your 13-year-old see 'Joker'?

00:02:19.438 --> 00:02:21.173
That's bad parenting."

00:02:21.173 --> 00:02:23.342
And I say, "It was genius.

00:02:23.342 --> 00:02:26.312
I enjoyed it
and my boy loved it.

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:28.280
Sometimes I do the wrong thing."

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:29.449
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.449 --> 00:02:32.018
-The first thing we went to
was Sea World

00:02:32.018 --> 00:02:35.321
and, you know, which we now know
is a terrible place for fish,

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:36.388
but, at the time,
we were okay with it.

00:02:36.388 --> 00:02:37.523
-At the time, we thought

00:02:37.523 --> 00:02:38.925
the fish loved it.
-Oh, god, they seemed

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:39.925
so happy!
-My parents told me

00:02:39.925 --> 00:02:41.260
the fish started it, yeah.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:43.395
[ Laughter ]
This was their idea, yeah.

00:02:43.395 --> 00:02:45.064
-Look, they're trying
to get out of the water

00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:46.532
and walk like us.

00:02:46.532 --> 00:02:47.867
-What does high crime mean?

00:02:47.867 --> 00:02:50.436
High doesn't mean high
in altitude.

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:53.539
It doesn't mean high
on good Colorado pot.

00:02:53.539 --> 00:02:55.607
-Sure, sure. 'Cause, most
of those, those are legal, now,

00:02:55.607 --> 00:02:56.909
so they're not even crimes.
-[laughing] Right.

00:02:56.909 --> 00:03:00.713
-I went outside to smoke
something legal in Colorado.

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:03.015
-We inhaled something there.

00:03:03.015 --> 00:03:04.049
I forget what it's called.

00:03:04.049 --> 00:03:06.518
We felt the effects
of that substance

00:03:06.518 --> 00:03:08.153
and then decided,
"You know what?

00:03:08.153 --> 00:03:09.288
We're all middle-aged.

00:03:09.288 --> 00:03:11.457
We should start
makin' music together."

00:03:11.457 --> 00:03:12.658
[ Laughter ]

00:03:12.658 --> 00:03:14.160
-I wrote these for Seth.

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.628
-Yeah.
-They're in Seth's voice.

00:03:15.628 --> 00:03:17.463
-No, they're not.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:18.898
